Chris Olah's blog and
the distill.pub journal

00:39:18.520 --> 00:39:21.490
that he started with
Shan Carter are really

00:39:21.490 --> 00:39:24.580
good expositions for people with
a certain level of expertise.

00:39:24.580 --> 00:39:27.610
I think there's things like the
Machine Learning Crash Course

00:39:27.610 --> 00:39:28.930
that Google put out.

00:39:28.930 --> 00:39:32.140
There's lots of courses
on Udacity and Coursera

00:39:32.140 --> 00:39:33.670
for different
levels of expertise.

00:39:33.670 --> 00:39:37.030
The deep learning textbook that
Ian Goodfellow, Yoshua Bengio,

00:39:37.030 --> 00:39:39.430
and Aaron Courville put
out is a very good one.

00:39:39.430 --> 00:39:41.290
There's lots of
material targeted

00:39:41.290 --> 00:39:43.300
at sort of people with
less advanced math

00:39:43.300 --> 00:39:46.450
skills for high school students
and middle school students,

00:39:46.450 --> 00:39:47.140
even.

00:39:47.140 --> 00:39:49.223
So there's just a wealth
of information out there,

00:39:49.223 --> 00:39:51.940
and it's really great that
the community is producing

00:39:51.940 --> 00:39:54.830
so much introductory material
and more advanced material

00:39:54.830 --> 00:39:55.480
for everyone.

